renderer: don't deref expired mirror weakptrs in damageMirrorsWith

CMonitor::m_mirrors is a std::vector<PHLMONITORREF> — weak references. When a
mirrored output goes away (DRM hotplug) the ref expires, but damageMirrorsWith
dereferences it unconditionally at the top of the loop:

    auto   monitor = mirror;
    double scale   = std::min(monitor->m_transformedSize.x / ..., ...);

so the next frame after the unplug faults on a null deref and takes the whole
session down. Confirmed against Hyprland 0.55.0 by disassembly:
damageMirrorsWith+0x338 is `movsd 0x60,%xmm0` (absolute-address load = null
plus the m_transformedSize offset) followed by `ud2`, i.e. GCC's codegen for a
path it proved was UB. Backtrace is always
damageMirrorsWith() <- renderMonitor() <- CMonitorFrameScheduler::onFrame().

The tail of the same loop already guards with `if (auto m = mirror.lock())`,
added upstream for 0.56.0 — but that is six lines past the fault, so the crash
survived. Lock once at the top and skip the mirror if it is gone.

Applies to Hyprland 52b368f1d7fdee1b0e96ef3dc655b5a577df4fdb (v0.56.0).

--- a/src/render/Renderer.cpp
+++ b/src/render/Renderer.cpp
@@ -2812,9 +2812,13 @@
 void IHyprRenderer::damageMirrorsWith(PHLMONITOR pMonitor, const CRegion& pRegion) {
     for (auto const& mirror : pMonitor->m_mirrors) {
 
-        // transform the damage here, so it won't get clipped by the monitor damage ring
-        auto    monitor = mirror;
+        // m_mirrors holds weak refs, so the mirror may already be gone (e.g. unplugged
+        // mid-frame on a hotplug). Dereferencing it below would be a null deref.
+        auto monitor = mirror.lock();
+        if (!monitor)
+            continue;
 
+        // transform the damage here, so it won't get clipped by the monitor damage ring
         CRegion transformed{pRegion};
 
         // we want to transform to the same box as in CHyprOpenGLImpl::renderMirrored
@@ -2826,10 +2830,8 @@
         transformed.scale(scale);
         transformed.translate(Vector2D(monbox.x, monbox.y));
 
-        mirror->addDamage(transformed);
-
-        if (auto m = mirror.lock())
-            m->scheduleFrame(Aquamarine::IOutput::AQ_SCHEDULE_DAMAGE);
+        monitor->addDamage(transformed);
+        monitor->scheduleFrame(Aquamarine::IOutput::AQ_SCHEDULE_DAMAGE);
     }
 }
 
